{"uid":"tools/fbench.py","name":"fbench.py","qualname":"tools/fbench.py","kind":"module","file":"tools/fbench.py","line":1,"end_line":130,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"fbench -- turn the PNG pairs `make parity` leaves behind into something you can act on.","description":"`make parity` prints one score per page. To fix a page you then need to SEE where the two\nengines part ways. This reads build/parity/<name>.fd.png (Freedom) and <name>.ff.png\n(Firefox) and, per page:\n  * writes build/bench/<name>.sbs.png: Freedom | Firefox side by side, cropped to the\n    band you ask for, so one Read shows the difference;\n  * prints the first row where the pictures diverge and the worst 100 px bands by mean\n    luminance difference, so you know which y to crop next;\n  * ranks the pages by score and shows the delta against tests/parity/baseline.tsv.\n\nUsage: fbench.py [--from Y] [--rows N] [--band PX] [page ...]\n  no page  -> every page that has a PNG pair\nRun `make fbench PAGES=\"a b\" FROM=1000 ROWS=800` to refresh the pair first.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["tools/fbench.py::PARITY","tools/fbench.py::OUT","tools/fbench.py::load_baseline","tools/fbench.py::load_current","tools/fbench.py::luma","tools/fbench.py::bands","tools/fbench.py::sbs","tools/fbench.py::main"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
